<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alberto Fujimori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a>–<a href="/years/2024">2024</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alberto Fujimori was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from 1990 to 2000. He curbed hyperinflation, closed Congress in a self-coup in 1992 and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shining-path">Shining Path</a> insurgency, whose leader was captured that year. He fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 2000 amid corruption scandals and was later convicted in Peru of human rights abuses and corruption.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alberto-fujimori.jpg" alt="Alberto Fujimori" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Lambiotte / European Communities, 1991 / EC - Audiovisual Service · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Visit_of_Alberto_Fujimori,_President_of_Peru,_to_the_CEC_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Alberto Kenya Fujimori Inomoto was born on 26 July 1938 in the Miraflores district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> to Japanese parents, Naoichi Fujimori and Mutsue Inomoto, who came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumamoto-prefecture">Kumamoto Prefecture</a> and had emigrated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> in 1934. Japanese was the language of the home, but his parents moved him in 1949 to a school taught only in Spanish so that their children could assimilate. He graduated first in his class in 1961 in agricultural engineering at the Universidad Nacional Agraria La Molina, studied physics in Strasbourg, and took a master's degree in mathematics at the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a>–Milwaukee in 1969. He became rector of La Molina in 1984 and held the post until 1989.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Career</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> was in hyperinflation and political crisis under the first presidency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alan-garcia">Alan García</a>, with the internal conflict against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shining-path">Shining Path</a> under way. Fujimori entered the 1990 election as an outsider under the banner of Cambio 90 and defeated the novelist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mario-vargas-llosa">Mario Vargas Llosa</a>. He became the country's first president of Japanese descent. His economic stabilisation programme, known as the Fujishock, used strict fiscal and monetary policy, deregulation and privatisation, and annual <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a> fell from a peak approaching 7,500 per cent to single digits by 1994.</p><p>In 1992 he dissolved Congress and the Supreme Court in a self-coup carried out with the support of the National Intelligence Service and the armed forces. The coup was criticised by many politicians and governments but welcomed by the business sector and much of the public. A new constitution was approved by referendum in 1993, and he was re-elected in 1995 and, controversially, in 2000. During his rule the army repressed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shining-path">Shining Path</a>, halting its actions while also killing thousands of civilians. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimiro-montesinos">Vladimiro Montesinos</a>, who headed the intelligence service, helped him to consolidate power.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Amid allegations of corruption and crimes against humanity, Fujimori went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 2000 and sent his resignation by fax. Congress refused it and voted to remove him. Japan declined to extradite him as a Japanese citizen. He was arrested in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> in 2005, extradited in 2007 and sentenced to 25 years in prison. President Pedro Pablo Kuczynski pardoned him in 2017, and he was released in December 2023; he died on 11 September 2024 of complications of tongue cancer. He has been described as a dictator, while a poll of 2005 found his years in office rated favourably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Alberto Fujimori” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Alberto Fujimori</b>, elected in 1990, closed Congress in his self-coup of April 1992 and introduced the 1993 constitution, still in force, which strengthened the presidency and created a single-chamber Congress; a return to two chambers was approved in 2024.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-peru">Republic of Peru · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In France the first president elected by universal male suffrage, Louis-Napoléon Bonaparte, barred from a second term, seized power in a coup in December 1851; in 1992 Peru’s president <b>Alberto Fujimori</b> closed Congress with the army’s support.</blockquote><a href="/government/presidential-democracy">Presidential democracy · Weaknesses</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Miraflores, in what is now <a href="/countries/peru">Peru</a>. Died in San Borja, in what is now <a href="/countries/peru">Peru</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-12.12,-77.03&amp;year=1993" aria-label="Miraflores on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2433 2615 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Alberto Fujimori"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2883 2885h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2883 2885h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-12.12,-77.03&amp;year=1993">What was here in 1993? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
